  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "rwJUurx85q9N1F6Ino+zggeKSTo=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:11.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Because reducers are pure, undo does not belong inside them. For each action you support, emit a paired *inverse* action that the app dispatches to roll the change back:\n\n```ts\nfunction invert(op: Operation): Action | null {\n  switch (op.type) {\n    case \"ADD_TODO\":      return removeTodo({ id: op.input.id });\n    case \"REMOVE_TODO\":   return addTodo({ id: op.input.id, title: op.input.restoreTitle });\n    case \"COMPLETE_TODO\": return uncompleteTodo({ id: op.input.id });\n    default:              return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\nDispatching the inverse produces a *new* operation in the log. You keep the history, the effect is undone, and nothing about the log is rewritten. Note what this forces on your schema: `REMOVE_TODO` can only be inverted if its input carries enough to reconstruct the item (hence `restoreTitle`). Designing for invertibility is a schema decision made when you specify the operation, not a feature you bolt on later.\n\n**Do not read this as \"the framework has no undo.\"** It does: `UNDO` and `REDO` are base document actions with input `{ count: Int }` (`packages/shared/document-model/types.ts`), implemented by `undoOperationV2` / `processUndoRedo` in the reducer core. That mechanism works by incrementing the index and marking the undone tail with `skip`, so consecutive NOOPs are collapsed during rebuild and garbage collection.\n\nThe two are different tools. Base `UNDO` is a generic \"take back the last N operations\" over the raw log. The inverse-action pattern is domain-level: it expresses the reversal as a first-class business event that peers, processors, and the audit trail all see as an intentional change. Reach for the inverse when the reversal is meaningful to the domain.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/02-Learn/08-deep-dives/01-reducers-in-depth.mdx; base UNDO/REDO confirmed in packages/shared/document-model/{types,operations,reducer}.ts (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:11.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:11.000Z"
    }
  },
